invariant: INV-22
file: handshake_record.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_test
reason: the blocking reader reads an alert in the clear only until its read
  key is installed, so a server that has sent its flight refuses the alert of
  a client that could not use the ServerHello as a record it cannot use and
  answers an alert that closed the connection. bin/tcp_blocking_loop_test
  requires ch_srv_accept to record the client's alert in the clear after its
  flight and to send nothing more.

--- old
        if (outer == REC_ALERT) {
            return hsr_refuse_alert(t, t->cfg.buf + part + REC_HDR, record_len - REC_HDR,
--- new
        if (outer == REC_ALERT && !h->encrypted) {
            return hsr_refuse_alert(t, t->cfg.buf + part + REC_HDR, record_len - REC_HDR,
